2026-09-14 | ... explicit coalesce | ar_001|rtl|NULL|f ; ar_SY|rtl|NULL|f ; en_US|ltr|true|t
2026-09-14 | ... "select count(*) total, count(*) filter (where active) active_count from res_lang;" | 93 | 1
2026-09-14 | which rtlcss | rtlcss: MISSING   (`npm ls -g --depth=0` -> claude-code, pi-coding-agent, opencode-ai, vercel, wasm-pack; no rtlcss)
2026-09-14 | ... users' language | __system__/en_US, admin/en_US, public/en_US, portaltemplate/en_US, demo/en_US, portal/en_US
2026-09-14 | OBSERVED | Phase E's premise is confirmed as fact, not assumption: the site's
                       "Arabic, right to left — live" badge is false. ar_001 and ar_SY carry
                       direction='rtl' but are NOT active, and rtlcss is absent so Odoo cannot
                       mirror any stylesheet (assetsbundle.run_rtlcss shells out to that binary).
2026-09-14 | NOTE | `res_lang.active` is a NULLABLE boolean and the Arabic rows hold **NULL**, not false.
                       Odoo's ORM reads NULL as "not active" (`active_test` matches active=true), so the
                       app behaves correctly — but a raw SQL check written as `where active = false`
                       or `where not active` will MISS these rows, because NULL fails both comparisons.
                       ACC-E02 (activating ar_001) and its verification must use `coalesce(active,false)`
                       or `active is true`, never `= false`. 93 languages exist; exactly 1 is active.

